      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Percutaneous treatment of coronary bifurcation lesions remains a challenging aspect of interventional cardiology, but the approach to trifurcation and quadrifurcation lesions can be considered \"double jeopardy.\" We describe two cases of trifurcation and one case of quadrifurcation that were treated percutaneously using a \"minimal protrusion balloon crush technique.\" Immediate and long-term results were favorable with this approach."},
